(SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE BOARD OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(DEPARTMENT OF DEBT AND HYBRID SECURITIES, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(SEBI/HO/DDHS/DDHS-PoD-1/P/CIR/2024/123) Tj
T*
(September 04, 2024) Tj
T*
(Master Circular for ESG Rating Providers \(ERPs\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Mandatory Registration: No person or entity shall act as an ESG Rating Provider \(ERP\) without obtaining a certificate of) Tj
T*
(registration from SEBI under the SEBI \(Credit Rating Agencies\) Regulations, 1999. ERPs are classified into Category I and Category II.) Tj
T*
(Category I ERPs must maintain a minimum net worth of rupees ten crore \(INR 10,00,000,000\), while Category II ERPs must maintain a) Tj
T*
(minimum net worth of rupees five crore.) Tj
T*
(2. Core ESG Ratings: Every ERP shall offer 'Core ESG Ratings' based strictly on verified parameters under the Business Responsibility) Tj
T*
(and Sustainability Reporting \(BRSR\) Core framework. Core ESG ratings must incorporate quantifiable indicators including greenhouse) Tj
T*
(gas footprint, water consumption intensity, waste management ratios, and gender diversity metrics.) Tj
T*
(3. Conflict of Interest Prohibitions: An ERP shall not provide consulting, advisory, or sustainability audit services to any company) Tj
T*
(for which it has issued or intends to issue an ESG rating. The rating committee must operate independently of business development.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 788 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(4. Disclosure of Methodologies and Scoring Models: ERPs must publish their ESG rating methodologies, sectoral weighting schemes,) Tj
T*
(and transition scoring models prominently on their websites. Any material modification in rating methodology must be disclosed to the) Tj
T*
(stock exchanges within three working days.) Tj
T*
(5. Rating Review and Retention: ESG ratings must be reviewed at least once every 12 months. All underlying analysis, data sheets, and) Tj
T*
(rating committee minutes must be preserved for a minimum period of five years following the withdrawal or expiry of the rating.) Tj
T*
(6. Rating Scale Standardization: ERPs shall adopt standardized nomenclature for ESG rating symbols to ensure comparability across providers.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 836 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(7. Environmental Pillar Parameters: The environmental evaluation under BRSR Core must assign weight to energy intensity per rupee) Tj
T*
(of turnover, percentage of energy consumed from renewable sources, absolute Scope 1 and Scope 2 emissions, and total water recycled.) Tj
T*
(8. Social Pillar Parameters: Under the social pillar, ERPs must evaluate employee median wage ratios, workforce health and safety incident) Tj
T*
(rates, percentage of female employees in senior management, and corporate social responsibility \(CSR\) project completion rates.) Tj
T*
(9. Governance Pillar Parameters: Governance assessments must examine board independence, presence of independent woman directors, executive) Tj
T*
(compensation link to sustainability targets, and audit committee compliance history.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Length 835 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(10. Subscriber-Pays vs Issuer-Pays Models: ERPs may operate under either subscriber-pays or issuer-pays business models. Under the) Tj
T*
(subscriber-pays model, rating reports are distributed only to accredited investors, but the summary rating score must be made publicly accessible.) Tj
T*
(11. Rating Appeals: An issuer dissatisfied with an ESG rating must be given an opportunity to present factual clarifications to the rating) Tj
T*
(committee within seven working days of rating communication.) Tj
T*
(12. Periodic Inspection by SEBI: SEBI reserves the right to conduct inspections of books of accounts, internal systems, and rating records) Tj
T*
(of any registered ERP at any time without prior notice.) Tj
T*
(Yours faithfully,) Tj
T*
(\(Pradeep Ramakrishnan\)) Tj
T*
(General Manager) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
